    description: "Pull PROJECT-SCOPED events from Google Calendar into events/*.yaml, filtered by manifest surfaces.google_calendar.harvest.keywords. Personal and other-project events are never imported. Idempotent; prunes previously imported events that fall out of scope.",
    prompt: `Sync PROJECT-SCOPED Google Calendar events into this project. The operator's calendar is a PERSONAL calendar shared across their whole life \u2014 most events on it do NOT belong to this project and importing them is a privacy violation.

SCOPE (read it first): manifest.yaml surfaces.google_calendar \u2014 calendar_id, and harvest.keywords (list), harvest.window_past_days (default 90), harvest.window_future_days (default 180), harvest.prune_out_of_scope (default true). If harvest.keywords is MISSING or empty, STOP and import nothing: report that the manifest needs surfaces.google_calendar.harvest.keywords before the calendar can be harvested. Never fall back to importing everything.

FILTER: an event is in scope ONLY if its title, description, or attendee list matches at least one keyword (case-insensitive; match short keywords like "pic" on word boundaries so "pick-up" does not match). Also treat events whose title starts with one of surfaces.google_calendar.event_prefixes as in scope (they are project-authored holds). Everything else is out of scope: do NOT write it to disk, do NOT list it in the activity log or your report, do NOT echo its title anywhere \u2014 count it silently and move on.

SYNC: using the Google Calendar MCP tools, fetch events for the window -window_past_days to +window_future_days from today. For each IN-SCOPE event, upsert events/<gcal_event_id>.yaml with fields: id (gcal-<gcal_event_id>), date (YYYY-MM-DD), time (HH:MM, omit if all-day), duration_min, title, description, attendees (email list), source: gcal, external: true, gcal_event_id, gcal_html_link, last_modified (ISO-8601).

CLEANUP: when harvest.prune_out_of_scope is true, delete events/*.yaml files with source: gcal whose content matches NO current keyword (a previous unscoped sync imported them). NEVER touch events without source: gcal \u2014 those are native project records.

AFTER: update state.json harvest_cursors.calendar to the current ISO timestamp; append one notifier.calendar-harvest event to logs/activity.ndjson with counts only (in_scope_upserted, out_of_scope_skipped, pruned). Report created/updated/unchanged/pruned counts and the number skipped as out of scope \u2014 counts only, no titles of skipped events.`
